  Magicbane's magic/curse resistance can make it superior to even
Grayswandir in melee.  The various lichs and "touch of death"
come to mind, not to mention their armor crumbling and cursing 
attacks.


  Judicious use of magic missile, as you point out, can almost
keep the player from ever fighting in melee.  But mana is a 
finite resource and has many other uses.  Using Magicbane to kill
weaker monsters in melee conserves mana.


  A +7 Magicbane can deal with stronger/more monsters than
+2 Magicbane.  That saves more Pwr.  (More popcorn monsters
can be windshielded, too.  But that's a minor pleasure.)


  There are equivalent options with armor.  Silver dragon scale 
mail is to a cloak of magic resistance as mid/high XL magic 
missile is to Magicbane.  The AC you get from the SDSM will 
always overshadow that from the CoMR.  You should still enchant 
up the CoMR.  (If more is better, too much is just right.)


  Alternatively, compare the Grayswandir/Magicbane options to the
CoProt/CoMR options.  The cloak of protection has three times as 
much base AC as the cloak of magic resistance.  If a player 
chooses the CoMR anyway, it should still be enchanted up.


  There is at least one case where doing more damage in melee
is silly, though:  when angering a peaceful foocubus.  (An 
angry foocubus will track your character down after teleporting
away.)  But the easy solution to that is to wield nothing: '-'.


  Finally, switching to Magicbane as the situation warrants,
as you seem to advocate, unnecessarily complicates the game,
imho.  One of the many nice things about playing wizards is the 
*lack* of choice about wielded weapon(s). ;^)  (Contrast that
with classes that can #twoweapon.)


  The good news, of course, is that wielding Magicbane doesn't
prevent you from performing the most damaging attacks in the
game.  So you can have your cake and eat it too.  

  Enchanting Magicbane to +7 is frosting on that cake, and can 
easily be a noticeable advantage in the early and middle game as 
well.








